%S A074003 1,0,3,9,30,81,225,756,2187,6561,19602,59049,177633,530712,1594323,
%T A074003 4782969,14351094,43046721,129127041,387440172,1162261467,3486784401,
%U A074003 10460294154,31381059609,94143533121,282429005040,847288609443,2541865828329,7625599079310
%N A074003 Number of elements of GF(3^n) with trace 1 and subtrace 0.
%C A074003 Same as the number of elements of GF(3^n) with trace 2 and subtrace 0.
%H A074003 Frank Ruskey, <a href="https://combos.org/TSGF3">Number of Elements of GF(3^n) with given trace and subtrace</a>.
%H A074003 Yang Xu, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22099040">A Proof of the Conjectured Recurrence for OEIS A074003</a> (2026).
%H A074003 <a href="/index/Rec#order_05">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (0,3,9,18,27).
%F A074003 From _Zhuorui He_, Oct 12 2025: (Start)
%F A074003 a(n) = 27*a(n-5) + 18*a(n-4) + 9*a(n-3) + 3*a(n-2) for n >= 6.
%F A074003 G.f.: (x + 3*x^5)/(1 - 3*x^2 - 9*x^3 - 18*x^4 - 27*x^5). (End)
%F A074003 The above recurrence and g.f. are proved in the linked note. - _Yang Xu_, Aug 25 2026
%o A074003 (SageMath)
%o A074003 def a(n):
%o A074003     if n==1: return 1
%o A074003     ans = 0
%o A074003     for x in GF(3^n):
%o A074003         if x.charpoly().coefficients(sparse=False)[-3:-1]==[0, 1]: ans += 1
%o A074003     return ans  # _Robin Visser_, Dec 28 2024
%Y A074003 Cf. A074000, A074001, A074002, A074004, A074005.
%K A074003 nonn,easy,changed
%O A074003 1,3
%A A074003 _Frank Ruskey_ and Nate Kube, Aug 19 2002
%E A074003 Terms a(13)-a(16) corrected, unverified terms a(17)-a(20) removed. Based on the original Data in A074000-A074005, a(17)-a(20) are possibly equal to 14351094, 43046721, 129127041, 387440172. - _Andrei Zabolotskii_, Nov 11 2024
%E A074003 Terms a(17)-a(20) recomputed and added again (verified that all the terms a(17)-a(20) conjectured by Andrei Zabolotskii are correct), and added term a(21). - _Robin Visser_, Dec 28 2024
%E A074003 a(22)-a(29) from _Yang Xu_, Aug 29 2026
